"The Materials" means everything in this repository and on the Jev Game Theory Lab
website, including source code, prompt designs, game designs, the experimental design
(for example the Hinted/Raw opponent modes, the Top pick/By odds move choices and the
calibration checks), documentation, text, graphics, and all gameplay data and
statistics collected or published by the project.

1. Permitted without asking
   a. Viewing and reading the Materials, and discussing them publicly.
   b. Running an unmodified copy locally, for personal, non-commercial evaluation only.
   c. Playing the games on the official website.
   d. Referring to or briefly quoting the project, with a citation (see CITATION.cff)
      and a link to the official repository.

2. Requires prior written permission from the authors
   a. Copying, modifying, adapting, translating or redistributing any part of the
      Materials, or publishing or hosting a derivative work or a public deployment.
   b. Using any part of the Materials — including the code, prompts, experimental
      design or data — in research, a thesis, a paper, a preprint, a benchmark,
      a dataset or any other publication.
   c. Collecting, scraping, downloading or re-analysing the gameplay data or
      statistics served by the project (including its /stats endpoint), or
      redistributing them.
   d. Training, fine-tuning or evaluating machine-learning models on the Materials.
   e. Any commercial use.

   To request permission or to collaborate, open an issue in the official repository.

3. Contributions
   By submitting a contribution (for example a pull request), you agree that it may be
